.gradle/
# Gradle output: the root project's, and EVERY module's. The per-module lines
# used to be spelled out one at a time, so adding :linuxapp dropped 484
# intermediates into `git status` — a wildcard is what keeps the next module
# from doing it again. Nothing in this repo is a tracked directory named build/
# (openandroiddex-wmd/build.sh is a file, and the trailing slash matches only
# directories), so the rule cannot swallow a source path.
openandroiddex-launcher/build/
openandroiddex-launcher/*/build/

# IDE, per-machine
.idea/
.vscode/

# Reverse-engineering scratch, local only. jadx/apktool output from a third-party
# closed-source product, plus our written analysis of it, kept as reference for the
# window-management and daemon work. It is someone else's compiled code decompiled
# and notes about someone else's product — neither is committed or redistributed.
# Nothing in this project is derived from it.
doc/decompiled-commercial-dex/
doc/decompiled-commercial-dex-v1.0/
doc/commercial-android-dex-architecture.md

# Android Studio writes this per machine and pins an absolute sdk.dir. It was
# committed once with a Windows path in it, which broke `npm run apk` on every
# other OS: Gradle prefers local.properties over ANDROID_HOME, so the build
# went looking for a C:\ drive. Set ANDROID_HOME instead.
local.properties

# Local research scratch: AOSP sources (adb, wifi, init) and saved
# android.googlesource.com pages kept while working out wireless ADB and the
# uid-2000 daemon. Someone else's Apache-2.0 code, read-only reference, and
# nothing in this project imports it — so it stays out of the repo.
/ADM.java
/AdbService.java
/wsc.java
/adb_mdns.h
/adb_utils.cpp
/commandline.cpp
/transport.h
/pm.cpp
/ss.cpp
/daemon_*.cpp
/init.rc
/adbd.rc
/adbd.te
/pc.txt
/shellmanifest.xml
/adbd.html
/adbdir.html
/apex.html
/rd.html
/root.html

# One-off machine setup with a hardcoded per-user path; not portable.
/_install_buildtools.cmd
